{
  "rules": [
    "Strong positive bias in true outcomes vs model: forecasts are systematically too low, especially in rising regimes; apply an upward level shift.",
    "Trend/acceleration underestimation: model captures direction but lags major upswings by ~3–10 days; increase responsiveness to recent momentum (higher weight on last 5–10 days).",
    "Horizon-dependent error: underprediction grows with lead time (small at days 1–3, large by days 10–30); use a ramping correction that increases with forecast horizon.",
    "Regime shift miss: when market breaks out (rapid rally), model continues to mean-revert around high-60s/low-70s; add a breakout detector that disables mean reversion and boosts slope after consecutive higher closes.",
    "Ceiling/anchoring effect: forecasts appear anchored near ~68–71 even as realized prices move into mid/high-70s and 80s; relax caps/priors and allow higher price states once new highs persist for several sessions.",
    "Post-spike behavior: model tends to fade strength too early (predicts pullbacks while realized continues higher); delay mean-reversion signals until momentum weakens (e.g., lower highs / negative returns over multiple days)."
  ]
}
